# Null Summoner, cast, enters: "if you cast it" holds (CR 603.4), so Bot2 reveals its hand (Lightning Bolt and Mountains) and
# Bot1 chooses a nonland card from it - a Mountain is refused, the Bolt (the positive control) is taken - and exiles it. Its
# threshold ability is a static ability (CR 604.1, 611.3a) that lets Bot1 cast that card only "as long as there are seven or
# more cards in your graveyard" (CR 207.2c): with one card there (the Black Lotus) and Mox Pearl's {W} open, the Bolt can't be
# cast. Brain Freeze, after five spells this turn, mills Bot1 eighteen cards (CR 702.40a); now the Bolt is cast from exile, its
# {R} paid with the Pearl's {W} because mana of any type can be spent to cast it (CR 609.4b). It hits Bot2 and, a card that
# left exile, goes to its owner's graveyard.

